cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PediBot — a paediatric answer with the source attached"
message: "If you use this software or its catalogue, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Beca
    given-names: Nicolás
    email: pedibot.ai@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/nicolasbeca/pedibot"
url: "https://pedibot.xyz"
abstract: >-
  PediBot answers parents' questions about a sick child using only what paediatric
  societies, health ministries and the WHO already publish for families, citing the
  document each sentence comes from. Rule-based triage runs before any model and puts the
  local emergency number first; a verification step rejects any draft without a valid
  citation, so when nothing in the corpus supports an answer the system says so instead of
  guessing. It ships emergency numbers for 90 countries, childhood vaccination schedules
  for 66, WHO growth standards, MUAC screening and paracetamol/ibuprofen dosing from fixed
  tables, in eight languages.
keywords:
  - paediatrics
  - child health
  - health information
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - open data
  - digital public good
  - multilingual
